1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,310
I'll be working this Christmas.
这个圣诞节我将去工作。

2
00:00:02,310 --> 00:00:03,490
My job?
我的工作？

3
00:00:03,490 --> 00:00:04,750
Santa Claus!
圣诞老人！

4
00:00:04,750 --> 00:00:08,090
White beard and red clothes are optional.
白胡子和红衣服是可选的。

5
00:00:08,090 --> 00:00:15,760
I'll be joining thousands of volunteers in Britain who go and help homeless and elderly people as well as poor children.
我将加入英国成千上万的志愿者队伍中，去帮助无家可归者、老年人以及贫困儿童。

6
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:18,760
Solidarity comes to life at this time of the year.
每年的这个时候，团结精神都会焕发生机。

7
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:21,370
It's cold and many people feel lonely.
天气寒冷，许多人感到孤独。

8
00:00:21,370 --> 00:00:23,010
I'll be there for them.
我会在那里陪伴他们。

9
00:00:23,010 --> 00:00:33,850
I was inspired by a woman in Scotland - Beatrice Cadell has just celebrated her 80th birthday and instead of presents for her, she asked her friends to buy toys.
我受到了一位苏格兰女性的启发——比阿特丽斯·卡德尔（Beatrice Cadell）刚刚庆祝了她的80岁生日，她没有要求朋友们送她礼物，而是让他们买玩具。

10
00:00:33,850 --> 00:00:40,420
They'll be donated to a toy bank - free toys for children whose parents can't afford to buy them any.
这些玩具将被捐赠给玩具银行——为那些父母买不起玩具的孩子们提供免费玩具。

11
00:00:40,420 --> 00:00:46,000
Cadell said: "Everyone that turned up to my birthday was absolutely brilliant!
卡德尔说：“出席我生日会的每个人都棒极了！

12
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:47,750
Somebody else can benefit.
其他人可以受益。

13
00:00:47,750 --> 00:00:48,960
We don't need it.
我们不需要这些。

14
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:50,320
We're old."
我们已经老了。”

15
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:54,300
There are plenty of places which welcome a helping hand at Christmas.
圣诞节期间有许多地方欢迎志愿者的帮助。

16
00:00:54,300 --> 00:01:03,460
The charity Crisis at Christmas, for example, has been looking for more than 10,000 volunteers to assist guests in their centres for homeless people.
例如，慈善机构“圣诞危机”（Crisis at Christmas）一直在寻找超过10,000名志愿者，来帮助其中心里无家可归的客人们。

17
00:01:03,460 --> 00:01:10,720
Volunteers with specialist skills like dentists, hairdressers, lorry drivers and performers are particularly welcome.
具有专业技能（如牙医、理发师、卡车司机和表演者）的志愿者尤其受欢迎。

18
00:01:10,720 --> 00:01:23,590
Another organisation, Community Christmas, is keen on volunteers who wish to offer companionship to lonely, elderly people on Christmas Day – it can be over a full lunch or just a cup of tea.
另一个组织“社区圣诞节”（Community Christmas）热衷于招募希望在圣诞节为孤独的老年人提供陪伴的志愿者——可以是一顿丰盛的午餐，也可以只是一杯茶。

19
00:01:23,590 --> 00:01:30,960
They have a website with a location page so that good Samaritans can register their interest in helping out and find out more.
他们网站提供一个地址页面，以便好心的乐善好施者可以登记他们的帮助意愿并了解更多信息。

20
00:01:30,960 --> 00:01:35,500
Scrooge is a character very much associated with this time of year.
斯克鲁奇（Scrooge）是一个与这个时节紧密相关的角色。

21
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:41,500
He's the central figure in A Christmas Carol, a classic by the English writer Charles Dickens.
他是英国作家查尔斯·狄更斯的经典作品《圣诞颂歌》中的核心人物。

22
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:45,270
Scrooge is a selfish man who only helps himself.
斯克鲁奇是一个自私自利的人。

23
00:01:45,270 --> 00:01:48,860
In the world of volunteering, there's no Scrooge in sight.
在志愿者的世界里，看不到斯克鲁奇的身影。

24
00:01:48,860 --> 00:01:51,120
We're all proud and happy Santas.
我们都是自豪而快乐的圣诞老人。

25
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:52,100
Merry Christmas!
圣诞快乐！
